From 666029538753d2581faed435655d8712a1e1a95d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 13:09:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools: give mktemp a template in generate_styles_string.sh

The script creates its XSLT stylesheet with a bare mktemp, which only
GNU and recent BSD versions accept. On macOS 10.6 mktemp requires a
template and prints its usage instead, so the variable stays empty,
xsltproc is asked to load "" for every style and the final rm exits 64
for want of an operand, killing the generation of styles_string.h.

Pass an explicit template under TMPDIR, which every mktemp understands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wUNQ69BaBcDfrxd6oXJeJ
---
 tools/generate_styles_string.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git tools/generate_styles_string.sh tools/generate_styles_string.sh
index 23d57e9..480f73f 100755
--- tools/generate_styles_string.sh
+++ tools/generate_styles_string.sh
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@ function get-l10n()
         done
 }
 
-SCR=$(mktemp)
+SCR=$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/darktable-styles.XXXXXX")
 
 echo '<?xml version="1.0"?>
          <xsl:stylesheet version="1.0"
-- 
